li.p:
It is possible that h is not continuous at x = -2, 0, 2,
since h is not differentiable at these points;
everywhere else, h must be continuous.

By definition, we know

  g'(0) & = \lim_{h \to 0} \frac{g(0+h) - g(0)}{h}
  & = \lim_{h \to 0} \frac{g(h) - g(0)}{h}
  & = \lim_{h \to 0} \frac{\sqrt{|h|} - \sqrt{|0|}}{h}
  & = \lim_{h \to 0} \frac{\sqrt{|h|}}{h}
